WEBVTT

00:00:00.703 --> 00:00:03.378
It seems today
that all you see

00:00:03.378 --> 00:00:06.715
Is violence in movies
and sex on TV

00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:10.676
But where are those
good old-fashioned values

00:00:10.676 --> 00:00:13.888
On which we used to rely?

00:00:13.888 --> 00:00:17.141
Lucky there's a family guy

00:00:17.141 --> 00:00:20.603
Lucky there's a man who
positively can do

00:00:20.603 --> 00:00:22.188
All the things
that make us

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:24.023
Laugh and cry!

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:29.070
He's a family guy!

00:00:33.699 --> 00:00:35.201
All right, now remember,
we're trash,

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.869
so no dressing rooms for us.

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:39.830
The Griffins are proud
middle-of-the-aisle
try-on people.

00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:42.667
Take a look, I don't care.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.377
Brian, I found our costume!

00:00:44.377 --> 00:00:46.045
We're gonna be Sonny and Cher!

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:47.755
And either one of us
could be Cher, I don't care--

00:00:47.755 --> 00:00:48.965
I guess I'll be Cher.

00:00:48.965 --> 00:00:50.299
How do you know
I don't already have plans

00:00:50.299 --> 00:00:52.343
-for Halloween?
-You do have plans.

00:00:52.343 --> 00:00:54.804
You're dressing as Sonny
and trick-or-treating with me.

00:00:56.055 --> 00:00:57.640
If you come near me,

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.017
you're saying you're okay
with getting hit!

00:01:00.017 --> 00:01:03.562
Yeah, everybody has a plan
until they see the husky kid

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:06.274
in the Halloween store
going absolutely nuts

00:01:06.274 --> 00:01:07.525
with nunchucks!

00:01:13.447 --> 00:01:14.907
This pumpkin's huge!

00:01:14.907 --> 00:01:16.867
-How'd you get it so big?
-Giggity.

00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:18.744
You guys promise not to laugh?

00:01:18.744 --> 00:01:20.037
-Oh, yeah, yeah.
-Yes.

00:01:20.037 --> 00:01:21.414
I wished for it.

00:01:23.457 --> 00:01:24.875
I knew you guys would laugh,

00:01:24.875 --> 00:01:27.378
but I also tended to it
for months.

00:01:27.378 --> 00:01:29.463
My only question is, why?

00:01:29.463 --> 00:01:30.965
Every year, I enter Quahog's

00:01:30.965 --> 00:01:32.633
Great Pumpkin
Halloween Contest

00:01:32.633 --> 00:01:36.095
and get creamed by that
dang Patrick McCloskey.

00:01:36.095 --> 00:01:37.972
Guy's got the best soil
in town.

00:01:37.972 --> 00:01:39.348
He's over there
on the east side.

00:01:39.348 --> 00:01:40.766
You know what that means.

00:01:40.766 --> 00:01:41.976
I think you know we don't.

00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:44.103
Closer to the coast,
more moisture.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.604
Should really be two contests,

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.356
one for each side of town.

00:01:47.356 --> 00:01:49.525
I think one's the right amount
of contests.

00:01:49.525 --> 00:01:50.693
Patrick McCloskey?

00:01:50.693 --> 00:01:52.236
Why do I know that name?

00:01:52.236 --> 00:01:54.196
Wait, weren't there
weird rumors about him
and Bonnie?

00:01:54.196 --> 00:01:55.531
No, it's just
the pumpkin thing.

00:01:59.243 --> 00:02:00.786
We are going to be
such a thing

00:02:00.786 --> 00:02:01.954
at trick-or-treating.

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.039
I'd honestly be Sonny

00:02:03.039 --> 00:02:04.957
if I wasn't exactly
Cher's size.

00:02:04.957 --> 00:02:06.417
I'm going to take
this costume off.

00:02:06.417 --> 00:02:08.210
Not yet, it's time for choreo!

00:02:08.210 --> 00:02:10.296
That's choreography.
Did you know that?

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.131
Stewie, I can't just spend
all day doing--

00:02:12.131 --> 00:02:14.133
So it's rock left,
rock right,

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:16.510
right elbow into chest,
half-air bump,

00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.138
left elbow into chest,
half-air bump.

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:20.389
Say it with me.

00:02:20.389 --> 00:02:22.266
Rock left, rock right,

00:02:22.266 --> 00:02:24.852
right elbow into chest,
half-air bump.

00:02:24.852 --> 00:02:26.771
You're off tempo.

00:02:26.771 --> 00:02:28.522
-Rock left, rock right...
-Left... right...

00:02:28.522 --> 00:02:31.150
-...right elbow into chest,
half-air bump.
-Chest... half...

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:32.777
-Bump.
-You're off tempo, again.

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:34.612
I'm starting to think
you don't really want this.

00:02:34.612 --> 00:02:35.780
I don't want this.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:37.490
Brian, do you know
how many Puerto Rican men

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:39.992
came here in giant sweatpants
to audition for me?

00:02:39.992 --> 00:02:41.577
You're taking this too far.

00:02:41.577 --> 00:02:43.871
I'm not getting bossed around
by you for the next two days.

00:02:43.871 --> 00:02:46.040
Well, now you know
how Cher felt about Sonny.

00:02:46.040 --> 00:02:48.042
I knew it was just
a matter of time

00:02:48.042 --> 00:02:49.668
until we became
the two of them.

00:02:49.668 --> 00:02:51.212
You look ridiculous,
by the way.

00:02:51.212 --> 00:02:52.421
How dare you?

00:02:52.421 --> 00:02:54.166
Rupert thinks I look amazing.

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:57.385
Well, great.
Rupert can be Sonny
because I'm done.

00:02:57.385 --> 00:02:58.678
I'm not taking you
trick-or-treating.

00:02:58.678 --> 00:02:59.970
I'm going to hang out
with my friends.

00:02:59.970 --> 00:03:01.972
Oh, your "friends," huh?
Name one.

00:03:01.972 --> 00:03:04.266
-Shut up.
-Oh, yeah, "Shut Up,"
great guy.

00:03:04.266 --> 00:03:05.976
I hate you!

00:03:05.976 --> 00:03:07.686
God, Brian's such a jerk.

00:03:07.686 --> 00:03:09.397
"Have Rupert be Sonny."

00:03:09.397 --> 00:03:11.607
You know what? Maybe I will.

00:03:11.607 --> 00:03:12.692
And here's your stupid

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.610
very-real-feeling
mustache back.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.404
Where do you even get
something like this?

00:03:16.404 --> 00:03:17.798
Don't worry
about where I got it.

00:03:18.521 --> 00:03:19.448
Hello?

00:03:19.692 --> 00:03:20.353
Where am I?

00:03:21.242 --> 00:03:22.243
Is anybody there?

00:03:25.204 --> 00:03:27.832
No!

00:03:33.254 --> 00:03:35.297
You guys
are big fact guys, right?

00:03:35.297 --> 00:03:38.217
I read Native Americans used
every part of the pumpkin.

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:41.429
It provided many gifts.
Clothing, soap, tools.

00:03:41.429 --> 00:03:43.639
Pumpkins were even honored
as relatives

00:03:43.639 --> 00:03:46.016
and paid tribute
to through songs,

00:03:46.016 --> 00:03:47.643
dance, and prayers.

00:03:47.643 --> 00:03:51.647
I am 100% sure
it's the buffalo
to which you are referring.

00:03:51.647 --> 00:03:53.732
Let's see
how the little guy's doing.

00:03:55.651 --> 00:03:57.361
A dark-eyed junco?

00:03:57.361 --> 00:03:59.113
That's a pumpkin
death sentence!

00:03:59.113 --> 00:04:00.322
Scram, scram!

00:04:00.322 --> 00:04:01.657
Get out of there! Bonnie?

00:04:01.657 --> 00:04:04.660
You out there? Get the broom!

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:06.579
What were we talking about?
Pumpkins?

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.247
Shut up about the pumpkin!

00:04:08.247 --> 00:04:09.915
I might give Bon a quick call.

00:04:09.915 --> 00:04:11.667
Make sure she knows
she's on bird duty.

00:04:13.127 --> 00:04:15.754
I apologize for my outburst.

00:04:15.754 --> 00:04:17.256
It's something I'm working on.

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:18.757
No apology necessary.

00:04:18.757 --> 00:04:21.302
I've had about all I can take
of this stupid pumpkin.

00:04:21.302 --> 00:04:23.053
Hey, what if we hid
Joe's pumpkin

00:04:23.053 --> 00:04:25.389
before it gets picked up
for the fair tomorrow morning?

00:04:25.389 --> 00:04:27.558
-I'm way in.
-Great idea, Peter.

00:04:27.558 --> 00:04:29.477
It's just a standard plan
of attack.

00:04:29.477 --> 00:04:31.979
Something I picked up
when I served at Fort Bragg.

00:04:31.979 --> 00:04:34.565
I once hit three homers
in a wiffle ball game.

00:04:34.565 --> 00:04:35.983
Why are you telling me this?

00:04:35.983 --> 00:04:37.109
Fort Bragg.

00:04:37.109 --> 00:04:39.069
You're going
to the war tomorrow.

00:04:39.069 --> 00:04:41.113
-Where is it?
-Afghanistan.

00:04:41.113 --> 00:04:43.365
I've been there,
like, four times, no big deal.

00:04:54.084 --> 00:04:56.504
All right, Rupert,
prepare to be brought to life

00:04:56.504 --> 00:04:58.464
to be my Sonny for Halloween.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.715
Oop, almost forgot.

00:05:03.594 --> 00:05:06.096
And finally,
this metal-studded dog collar

00:05:06.096 --> 00:05:07.306
to conduct electricity,

00:05:07.306 --> 00:05:08.891
and not because it's
my biggest kink.

00:05:13.896 --> 00:05:15.648
Did the Internet just go out?

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:16.899
It won't be long!

00:05:16.899 --> 00:05:18.526
Yeah, it's out.

00:05:18.526 --> 00:05:20.861
Guys, you can go,
like, two seconds
without the Internet!

00:05:47.263 --> 00:05:48.514
It's not alive.

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:50.683
It's not alive!

00:05:54.603 --> 00:05:56.063
Internet's back for me.

00:05:56.063 --> 00:05:59.066
Me too.
Reebok.com, baby!

00:06:03.487 --> 00:06:05.322
One, two, three!

00:06:07.783 --> 00:06:09.743
-Where are we taking this?
-I don't know.

00:06:09.743 --> 00:06:11.620
What?
I thought you had a plan!

00:06:11.620 --> 00:06:13.664
Yeah, the plan,
which everyone loved,

00:06:13.664 --> 00:06:15.040
was to hide the pumpkin.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:17.209
Oh, for crying out loud.

00:06:17.209 --> 00:06:18.919
Am I the only one
who can make plans?

00:06:18.919 --> 00:06:20.629
I have decision fatigue.

00:06:21.338 --> 00:06:22.756
Uh-oh.

00:06:22.756 --> 00:06:24.174
We wrecked Joe's pumpkin.

00:06:24.174 --> 00:06:25.843
And my sneakers!

00:06:27.928 --> 00:06:29.221
Cleveland, are you--

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:30.431
Are those Yeezys?

00:06:30.431 --> 00:06:31.849
They're cheaper now.

00:06:36.729 --> 00:06:37.730
Rupert?

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:39.440
Rupert?

00:06:40.566 --> 00:06:42.401
Rupert, you awake?

00:06:42.401 --> 00:06:43.694
Oh, good, you are.

00:06:43.694 --> 00:06:44.945
Yes, it's about Brian.

00:06:44.945 --> 00:06:46.196
He was so mean.

00:06:46.196 --> 00:06:48.824
I can't believe he just
ditched me on Halloween.

00:06:48.824 --> 00:06:51.201
He's my best friend,
and this is how he treats me.

00:06:51.201 --> 00:06:52.017
I hate him.

00:06:52.134 --> 00:06:53.787
Seriously,
I wish he were dead.

00:06:53.787 --> 00:06:55.539
I mean it,
no takesies-backsies.

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:57.374
Good night, Rupert.

00:06:58.751 --> 00:06:59.877
Rupert?

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:01.045
Rupert, you awake?

00:07:01.045 --> 00:07:02.171
Oh, good, you're awake.

00:07:02.171 --> 00:07:03.172
Good night.

00:07:10.721 --> 00:07:13.098
Dear Stewie,
you've given me life,

00:07:13.098 --> 00:07:15.476
and some would say
I'm indebted to you.

00:07:15.476 --> 00:07:17.561
Well, I don't know
if all that's true,

00:07:17.561 --> 00:07:21.482
but you've got me,
and, baby, I've got you.

00:07:24.902 --> 00:07:27.863
And now to fulfill your wish,

00:07:27.863 --> 00:07:31.659
I must kill Brian.

00:07:31.659 --> 00:07:35.579
But first, I must kill
this bag of Doritos.

00:07:35.579 --> 00:07:38.374
Family Guy. It was either this
or we fire three writers.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:48.408
Step aside.

00:07:48.408 --> 00:07:50.410
Now, let's remember,
it's just a pumpkin.

00:07:53.789 --> 00:07:56.166
No, no, no!
We can put it back together.

00:07:56.166 --> 00:07:57.793
Are you telling me
you can do

00:07:57.793 --> 00:08:00.295
what the Humpty Dumpty
crew couldn't?

00:08:00.295 --> 00:08:02.422
I-- I never got
to the end of that.

00:08:02.422 --> 00:08:04.383
And you have no king's horses,

00:08:04.383 --> 00:08:07.010
and they had
all the King's horses.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.138
I'm not sure how much horses
can help fix a broken egg guy.

00:08:10.138 --> 00:08:12.349
Yeah, good luck
with those hooves.

00:08:13.517 --> 00:08:14.810
Well, I'm finished.

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:17.312
May as well give McCloskey
the trophy now.

00:08:17.312 --> 00:08:19.189
You know,
the damage is on the bottom.

00:08:19.189 --> 00:08:21.650
We can just shovel
the rest of the goop
back in and prop it up.

00:08:21.650 --> 00:08:25.529
We can't just scoop 307 pounds
of pumpkin guts in there.

00:08:31.743 --> 00:08:34.329
307 pounds is my exact weight.

00:08:34.329 --> 00:08:36.373
This is crazy, but I think
I could slide in

00:08:36.373 --> 00:08:37.666
through the hole
in the bottom.

00:08:37.666 --> 00:08:39.459
Then I could just sit in there
for a few hours,

00:08:39.459 --> 00:08:41.169
and maybe you can
still win the contest.

00:08:41.169 --> 00:08:42.504
You'd do that for me?

00:08:42.504 --> 00:08:43.922
I broke it. I'll fix it.

00:08:43.922 --> 00:08:45.799
Plus, I want to beat McCloskey
for you.

00:08:45.799 --> 00:08:47.009
I heard about him and Bonnie.

00:08:47.009 --> 00:08:48.468
I don't know
what people are hearing.

00:08:48.468 --> 00:08:49.928
It's just pumpkin stuff
with us.

00:08:54.099 --> 00:08:56.935
Welcome to the Quahog
Great Pumpkin Contest.

00:08:56.935 --> 00:08:58.270
We're going to start today

00:08:58.270 --> 00:09:00.021
with the pumpkin pie
eating event.

00:09:00.021 --> 00:09:02.190
Peter Griffin is
our reigning champion.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:05.152
Peter, come on up and accept
this Pie to the City.

00:09:05.152 --> 00:09:07.320
Joe, I need
to come out for a minute.

00:09:07.320 --> 00:09:08.864
It's too risky, Peter.

00:09:08.864 --> 00:09:11.324
The Pie to the City
enables the bearer

00:09:11.324 --> 00:09:13.493
to go to any establishment
with pie

00:09:13.493 --> 00:09:16.413
and get a free pie
at any time.

00:09:16.413 --> 00:09:17.873
Sorry, bud.

00:09:17.873 --> 00:09:19.124
We'll get you pie later.

00:09:39.978 --> 00:09:41.229
-Who is that?
-Who was that?

00:09:41.229 --> 00:09:42.439
That's the king.

00:09:42.439 --> 00:09:43.565
That's McCloskey.

00:09:43.565 --> 00:09:45.400
He's allowed to just park
on the grass?

00:09:45.400 --> 00:09:46.651
They'll ask him to move.

00:09:46.651 --> 00:09:47.986
That's what they did
last year.

00:09:52.240 --> 00:09:54.034
Stewie thinks
I have no friends.

00:09:54.034 --> 00:09:55.243
Then what are all these?

00:09:56.161 --> 00:09:57.621
Hello, Brian.

00:09:57.621 --> 00:10:00.332
Enjoy your last call.

00:10:03.335 --> 00:10:04.477
Hello?

00:10:04.502 --> 00:10:07.672
Sanfo, what do we got going on
for All Hallows' Eve?

00:10:07.672 --> 00:10:08.757
Hang sesh?

00:10:08.757 --> 00:10:09.841
Who is this?

00:10:09.841 --> 00:10:11.218
Bri-guy, from the line.

00:10:11.218 --> 00:10:12.302
What line?

00:10:12.302 --> 00:10:13.720
"What line," he says.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.055
Maverick.

00:10:15.055 --> 00:10:18.099
Uh, dude, that was,
like, three years ago.

00:10:18.099 --> 00:10:19.184
Ha! What're we
gettin' into tonight,

00:10:19.184 --> 00:10:21.186
you ol' bull shark?

00:10:21.186 --> 00:10:22.562
I don't know, man.

00:10:22.562 --> 00:10:24.856
I might go
to the Quahog Cemetery
outdoor movie.

00:10:24.856 --> 00:10:25.941
Love it. Should we get

00:10:25.941 --> 00:10:28.151
the Dime Boys involved
is the question?

00:10:28.151 --> 00:10:30.362
Hey, while I got ya,
let me show you my yard.

00:10:30.362 --> 00:10:32.405
So much potench.

00:10:32.405 --> 00:10:34.282
Ugh. "Potench."

00:10:34.282 --> 00:10:36.117
Now I want to kill him twice.

00:10:40.914 --> 00:10:41.998
Look at him.

00:10:41.998 --> 00:10:43.375
He's so cool.

00:10:43.375 --> 00:10:45.293
I want to see him
so bad.

00:10:47.796 --> 00:10:48.964
Hoo-hoo-hoo!

00:10:48.964 --> 00:10:51.675
Look who it is,
"Second Place" Swanson.

00:10:51.675 --> 00:10:53.176
That nickname
doesn't make sense

00:10:53.176 --> 00:10:55.178
because one year
I was sixth place.

00:10:55.178 --> 00:10:57.055
Feel stupid now, McCloskey?

00:10:57.055 --> 00:10:59.599
Let me get a closer look
at your pumpkin.

00:10:59.599 --> 00:11:01.726
Could barely see it
from over there.

00:11:01.726 --> 00:11:03.770
Ha, classic McCloskey.

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:05.547
-What was that?
-What?

00:11:05.547 --> 00:11:08.550
All I hear are whispers
from all the pumpkin bloggers

00:11:08.550 --> 00:11:10.885
saying McCloskey's reign
is over.

00:11:10.885 --> 00:11:11.970
Good news.

00:11:11.970 --> 00:11:13.305
When your pumpkin loses,

00:11:13.305 --> 00:11:14.764
you can still use it
as a centerpiece

00:11:14.764 --> 00:11:16.307
at Thanksgiving.

00:11:16.307 --> 00:11:18.643
Provided you have
a small enough table.

00:11:18.643 --> 00:11:20.061
Hey, hey, hey, hey!

00:11:20.061 --> 00:11:21.980
It's not worth it.
None of this is.

00:11:21.980 --> 00:11:23.231
I wish I stayed home.

00:11:26.484 --> 00:11:30.655
And this year's Quahog
Great Pumpkin winner is...

00:11:34.117 --> 00:11:36.036
It's just pumpkin stuff, Joe.

00:11:36.036 --> 00:11:37.162
Oh, good.

00:11:37.162 --> 00:11:38.830
See, fellas? Pumpkin stuff.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:40.749
Joe Swanson!

00:11:40.749 --> 00:11:42.834
-Yeah! Mwah.
-Ugh!

00:11:42.834 --> 00:11:45.003
Better luck next year,
McCloskey.

00:11:45.754 --> 00:11:46.838
What are they doing?

00:11:48.131 --> 00:11:50.383
All the Pumpkin County winners
are entered

00:11:50.383 --> 00:11:52.427
in the State Halloween Contest
in Providence.

00:11:52.427 --> 00:11:55.513
Do you know anything about
regional pumpkin contests?

00:11:55.513 --> 00:11:58.308
Oh, suck my bumpy gourd,
McCloskey.

00:11:58.308 --> 00:11:59.517
Your what?

00:11:59.517 --> 00:12:01.519
My bumpy little orange,
green, and yellow

00:12:01.519 --> 00:12:04.064
Gonzo-nose-shaped gourd.

00:12:04.064 --> 00:12:05.148
Stop describing it.

00:12:06.941 --> 00:12:08.193
Are we driving?

00:12:08.193 --> 00:12:09.986
I don't have a seat belt.

00:12:09.986 --> 00:12:11.321
Trick-or-treat!

00:12:16.826 --> 00:12:19.329
Weird. That kid looks like
your teddy bear.

00:12:19.329 --> 00:12:20.747
Except he's holding
a big knife

00:12:20.747 --> 00:12:23.041
and has a present-day
Anthony Kiedis costume.

00:12:26.169 --> 00:12:28.379
That's not present-day
Anthony Kiedis.

00:12:28.379 --> 00:12:29.672
That's Sonny Bono.

00:12:29.672 --> 00:12:31.424
Oh, my God, it worked!

00:12:31.424 --> 00:12:33.760
I made life! Yay!

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:37.055
Rupert, you're alive!

00:12:37.055 --> 00:12:38.431
Thanks to you.

00:12:38.431 --> 00:12:41.101
This is amazing! Oh,
we have so much to talk about.

00:12:41.101 --> 00:12:42.644
But first, candy.

00:12:42.644 --> 00:12:44.229
I can't wait to join you,

00:12:44.229 --> 00:12:48.399
right after I find
and kill Brian, babe.

00:12:48.399 --> 00:12:49.526
Wait, what?

00:12:49.526 --> 00:12:52.487
Remember?
"I wish Brian were dead."

00:12:52.487 --> 00:12:54.197
Oh, I was just angry
for a second.

00:12:54.197 --> 00:12:56.241
But forget all that.
You're alive!

00:12:56.241 --> 00:12:57.492
Let's trick-or-treat.

00:12:57.492 --> 00:12:58.660
Of course.

00:12:58.660 --> 00:13:00.411
Once I kill Brian.

00:13:00.411 --> 00:13:02.038
Come on, Rupert.
Don't be silly.

00:13:02.038 --> 00:13:03.248
I'm not mad anymore.

00:13:03.248 --> 00:13:05.041
Actually, I like being
a solo act.

00:13:05.041 --> 00:13:08.586
I got an Oscar and, like,
100 hot young boyfriends
ahead of me.

00:13:08.586 --> 00:13:11.214
Gonna do a fishnet dance
on an aircraft carrier,

00:13:11.214 --> 00:13:13.383
remind our boys in white
what they're fightin' for.

00:13:13.383 --> 00:13:14.884
Anyway,
you don't have to kill him.

00:13:14.884 --> 00:13:17.303
But you said,
"No takesies-backsies."

00:13:19.264 --> 00:13:21.015
Rupert, where did you go?

00:13:21.015 --> 00:13:23.226
Oh, my God,
I have to save Brian!

00:13:24.978 --> 00:13:27.105
Mr. Herbert,
you're trick-or-treating?

00:13:27.105 --> 00:13:28.982
Oh, I use Halloween
to take care of

00:13:28.982 --> 00:13:31.025
a little yearly housekeeping.

00:13:33.303 --> 00:13:34.387
Trick-or-treat!

00:13:34.387 --> 00:13:36.473
I'm a registered sex offender.

00:13:41.269 --> 00:13:42.270
Brian!

00:13:42.854 --> 00:13:44.105
Brian!

00:13:44.105 --> 00:13:45.648
Where could he be?

00:13:45.648 --> 00:13:46.858
Hey, Cher!

00:13:46.858 --> 00:13:48.818
Hey, guys!

00:13:48.818 --> 00:13:50.278
I'm putting this on Instagram!

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:52.697
Well, this is a big hit.

00:13:52.697 --> 00:13:54.574
I can't stop smiling.

00:13:54.574 --> 00:13:56.201
Instagram! Of course!

00:13:56.201 --> 00:13:57.577
Brian doesn't have
the confidence

00:13:57.577 --> 00:13:59.204
not to shove
every sad little thing

00:13:59.204 --> 00:14:00.622
he does down our throats.

00:14:00.777 --> 00:14:01.557
Bingo!

00:14:01.597 --> 00:14:03.750
He's going to watch
an '80s horror boob movie

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:04.918
at the cemetery.

00:14:04.918 --> 00:14:07.045
"Gonna be cool
to see them so big."

00:14:07.045 --> 00:14:09.047
Hashtag big screen boobs.

00:14:09.047 --> 00:14:11.716
"Waiting on my guy Sanfo
with the provisions."

00:14:11.716 --> 00:14:14.803
Parenthetical,
"All the Jameson, please.
LOL."

00:14:14.803 --> 00:14:16.471
Ugh, what a mess.

00:14:16.471 --> 00:14:18.073
Shall we split a cab?

00:14:18.681 --> 00:14:20.892
It's nice he's
at the cemetery.

00:14:20.892 --> 00:14:22.477
Less clean up.

00:14:27.273 --> 00:14:28.483
God, that's awful.

00:14:34.697 --> 00:14:36.366
Peter's been in that pumpkin
all day.

00:14:36.366 --> 00:14:37.826
We gotta find him
and get him out.

00:14:39.369 --> 00:14:42.080
It's going to take us hours
with all these pumpkins.

00:14:42.080 --> 00:14:43.206
- Peter!
- Yeah?

00:14:43.206 --> 00:14:44.999
-Oh, wow.
-Can I come out?

00:14:44.999 --> 00:14:46.209
I should be at work.

00:14:46.209 --> 00:14:47.710
Yeah, let's get you
out of there.

00:14:47.710 --> 00:14:49.087
Well, well, well.

00:14:49.087 --> 00:14:50.630
"Miracle-Grow" Joe.

00:14:50.630 --> 00:14:52.382
McCloskey,
what are you doing here?

00:14:52.382 --> 00:14:54.300
I saved my wristband
from last year.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:55.927
They didn't change the color.

00:14:55.927 --> 00:14:58.054
I didn't ask how you got in.

00:14:58.054 --> 00:14:59.681
Well,
something doesn't add up.

00:14:59.681 --> 00:15:02.392
Last year,
your pumpkin was 18 pounds.

00:15:02.392 --> 00:15:05.562
And this year, it's 307?

00:15:05.562 --> 00:15:08.022
Seems like
a disproportionate step up.

00:15:08.022 --> 00:15:09.232
But what do I know?

00:15:09.232 --> 00:15:12.277
Just almost every
pumpkin thing there is.

00:15:12.277 --> 00:15:13.653
Get lost, McCloskey.

00:15:13.653 --> 00:15:16.156
Oh, ho-ho-ho!
No, I'm sticking around.

00:15:16.156 --> 00:15:17.782
I'm gonna get
to the bottom of this.

00:15:17.782 --> 00:15:21.703
Yeah, now I'm kind of
wondering myself.

00:15:21.703 --> 00:15:24.205
Hello, hipsters
and newly-sober people

00:15:24.205 --> 00:15:26.833
who ran out of
seltzer flavors to try.

00:15:26.833 --> 00:15:29.085
The movie will start soon.

00:15:29.085 --> 00:15:31.462
Do you mind if I scoot
your blanket over a bit?

00:15:31.462 --> 00:15:32.714
You're on my dad's grave,

00:15:32.714 --> 00:15:34.257
and I'd like to leave
these flowers.

00:15:34.257 --> 00:15:36.176
I totally get it
from your perspective,

00:15:36.176 --> 00:15:38.636
but Sanfo should be here
in uno momento,

00:15:38.636 --> 00:15:40.763
and there's a chance
the Dime Boys may roll,

00:15:40.763 --> 00:15:41.931
so, yeah, no.

00:15:46.102 --> 00:15:47.562
Hello.

00:15:47.562 --> 00:15:49.147
Do you mind if I sit?

00:15:49.147 --> 00:15:52.233
Whoa, a kid dressed as a bear
dressed as Sonny Bono?

00:15:52.233 --> 00:15:53.318
That's so weird.

00:15:53.318 --> 00:15:54.944
Oh, how so?

00:15:54.944 --> 00:15:56.905
Just-- I was supposed to go
as that.

00:15:56.905 --> 00:15:58.239
Well, why didn't you?

00:15:58.239 --> 00:16:00.283
Maybe somebody
was counting on you.

00:16:00.283 --> 00:16:01.868
Oh, that's not him.

00:16:01.868 --> 00:16:03.661
Sorry, bud.
I'm sorta keeping an eye out
for my friends.

00:16:03.661 --> 00:16:05.288
They'll probably need help
with the YETI.

00:16:05.288 --> 00:16:07.999
It's the big one. Not cheap,
but heirloom quality.

00:16:07.999 --> 00:16:12.629
You know, to have a friend,
you must first be a friend.

00:16:12.629 --> 00:16:15.506
And you haven't been
a very good one, have you?

00:16:15.506 --> 00:16:16.591
Hey, you got it, Sonny.

00:16:16.591 --> 00:16:17.842
Hey, I'm gonna run
to the bathroom.

00:16:17.842 --> 00:16:19.802
If you see three guys
dressed as Anchorman

00:16:19.802 --> 00:16:21.262
scream-quoting Will Ferrell,

00:16:21.262 --> 00:16:23.139
tell 'em this is the spot.

00:16:23.139 --> 00:16:26.351
Oh, this is the spot,
all right.

00:16:26.351 --> 00:16:28.645
The spot to die.

00:16:30.647 --> 00:16:31.856
We gotta get
Peter out of there.

00:16:31.856 --> 00:16:32.982
He's starting to lose it.

00:16:32.982 --> 00:16:34.776
Something is off
with this pumpkin.

00:16:34.776 --> 00:16:36.653
Don't hate me
'cause you ain't me.

00:16:36.653 --> 00:16:39.530
McCloskey said that to me
last year and now I say it.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:42.283
I have to go to the bathroom
more than the pail in here!

00:16:42.283 --> 00:16:44.244
Mr. Swanson,

00:16:44.244 --> 00:16:45.703
what is going on here?

00:16:45.703 --> 00:16:47.580
I'm sorry.

00:16:47.580 --> 00:16:48.748
I've disgraced--

00:16:48.748 --> 00:16:50.208
I also have to go
to the bathroom

00:16:50.208 --> 00:16:51.793
more than the pail in here!

00:16:51.793 --> 00:16:53.628
Who is that?

00:16:53.628 --> 00:16:55.588
We all have to go
to the bathroom

00:16:55.588 --> 00:16:57.423
more than the pail in here!

00:16:57.423 --> 00:16:59.717
My wife made me volunteer
for this job.

00:16:59.717 --> 00:17:01.135
I'm not really sure
what to do.

00:17:01.135 --> 00:17:03.221
Maybe we just vote
on the fattest guy?

00:17:03.221 --> 00:17:04.847
This seems mean now.

00:17:04.847 --> 00:17:06.557
How'd you know I was cheating?

00:17:06.557 --> 00:17:07.892
The truth is...

00:17:07.892 --> 00:17:10.436
there's no way
to win this contest clean.

00:17:10.436 --> 00:17:12.480
No real pumpkin
is ever over 20 pounds.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:13.856
But yours always are.

00:17:13.856 --> 00:17:16.609
My fat son sits in mine
every year.

00:17:16.609 --> 00:17:19.445
All these years,
I thought giant pumpkins

00:17:19.445 --> 00:17:20.989
were just full of seeds.

00:17:20.989 --> 00:17:22.448
Forget it, Joe.

00:17:22.448 --> 00:17:24.033
It's Pumpkin Town.

00:17:36.754 --> 00:17:38.381
I gotta put
some thought to this,

00:17:38.381 --> 00:17:40.675
but I think I may be in love
with that guy.

00:17:45.138 --> 00:17:46.681
Have you seen a dog
with a bear

00:17:46.681 --> 00:17:48.099
in a Sonny Bono costume?

00:17:49.350 --> 00:17:51.227
No, nothing like that.

00:17:51.227 --> 00:17:52.520
Just a dog with a bear

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:54.188
in a present-day
Anthony Kiedis costume.

00:17:57.525 --> 00:17:59.152
That's him!
Which way did they go?

00:18:05.158 --> 00:18:07.285
Oh, God, I'm too late.

00:18:07.285 --> 00:18:08.411
You're not too late!

00:18:08.411 --> 00:18:09.912
But by the time
I start helping,

00:18:09.912 --> 00:18:11.164
don't you think
it'll be too late?

00:18:11.164 --> 00:18:13.333
Not at all. Help!

00:18:23.835 --> 00:18:25.123
You should go.

00:18:25.201 --> 00:18:28.006
I don't think
you'll want to see
what happens next.

00:18:28.006 --> 00:18:30.300
I command you
not to kill Brian.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:33.386
Dear, dear, Stewie,
don't you see it?

00:18:33.386 --> 00:18:34.929
You only animated me to life

00:18:34.929 --> 00:18:37.515
when Brian said
he wouldn't be Sonny.

00:18:37.515 --> 00:18:41.394
You turn to me only when
Brian's mean to you.

00:18:41.394 --> 00:18:43.688
I'm always second to him.

00:18:43.688 --> 00:18:44.772
Well, that's not true.

00:18:44.772 --> 00:18:45.898
Isn't it?

00:18:45.898 --> 00:18:48.526
Do you know
my name's not even Rupert?

00:18:48.526 --> 00:18:49.694
It's Jerry.

00:18:49.694 --> 00:18:51.779
Ugh, I've been hanging out
with a Jerry?

00:18:51.779 --> 00:18:55.241
But once Brian's gone,
I'll finally be first.

00:18:55.241 --> 00:18:59.037
You're one and only
best friend.

00:19:16.054 --> 00:19:18.306
Say you'll leave Brian alone,
and I'll let you go.

00:19:19.057 --> 00:19:21.100
I can't do that.

00:19:21.100 --> 00:19:26.230
In that case,
you leave me no choice.

00:19:28.107 --> 00:19:31.194
If I could turn back time

00:19:31.194 --> 00:19:34.405
If I could find a way

00:19:34.405 --> 00:19:38.159
I'd take back those words
that have hurt you

00:19:38.159 --> 00:19:40.578
And you'd stay

00:19:46.667 --> 00:19:48.544
What's... what's happening?

00:19:48.544 --> 00:19:49.879
Oh, hey, man.

00:19:49.879 --> 00:19:51.339
How much did you hear?

00:19:51.339 --> 00:19:53.341
You brought your bear to life
and told him to kill me?

00:19:53.341 --> 00:19:55.093
Damn, I was hoping
you missed that.

00:19:55.093 --> 00:19:58.763
Also, you chose me
and saved my life.

00:19:58.763 --> 00:20:00.681
You're my best friend, Bri.

00:20:00.681 --> 00:20:02.850
I'm really sorry
I put you through this.

00:20:02.850 --> 00:20:04.936
Eh, I was pretty selfish, too.

00:20:04.936 --> 00:20:06.854
I should have made time
to take my best friend

00:20:06.854 --> 00:20:07.980
trick-or-treating.

00:20:07.980 --> 00:20:09.732
I'm your best friend?

00:20:09.732 --> 00:20:11.317
You're pretty much
my only friend.

00:20:12.652 --> 00:20:14.862
What about Sanfo
and the Dime Boys?

00:20:14.862 --> 00:20:18.282
Honestly, I think Sanfo's just
using me for my sick yard.

00:20:18.282 --> 00:20:19.992
Happy Halloween, Bri,

00:20:19.992 --> 00:20:21.577
you total loon.

00:20:21.577 --> 00:20:22.995
Happy Halloween, Stewie.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:32.380
Man, that yard is going to be
the place to be this summer.

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:34.632
Maybe this is the summer
I get back into croquet.

00:20:34.632 --> 00:20:35.800
We do have the space.

00:20:35.800 --> 00:20:37.343
Yeah, lot of potench.

00:20:37.343 --> 00:20:38.344
Ugh.

00:20:45.143 --> 00:20:47.103
Oh, I know what you want.

00:20:47.812 --> 00:20:49.272
Here you go, sweetie.

00:20:49.272 --> 00:20:52.108
Your fluffy little friend
is all dry and good as new.

00:20:54.485 --> 00:20:55.903
Well, you lost a little stank,

00:20:55.903 --> 00:20:57.488
but that should come back
in time.

00:20:57.488 --> 00:21:00.283
Oh, my God, Rupert,
you would not believe
what happened.

00:21:00.283 --> 00:21:03.327
I animated you to life,
and then you decided to kill--

00:21:03.327 --> 00:21:05.288
Yes, to life! Me!

00:21:05.288 --> 00:21:08.332
I did it, and then you decided
to kill Brian, because--

00:21:08.332 --> 00:21:09.876
No, we do not wish
he was dead.

00:21:09.876 --> 00:21:11.836
Not anymore, at least.
And then...

00:21:11.836 --> 00:21:14.672
What on earth
do they talk about?